          <data key="d101">Protein kinase B; Protein kinase B alpha; Proto-oncogene c-Akt; RAC-PK-alpha</data>
          <data key="d104">AKT1 is one of 3 closely related serine/threonine-protein kinases (AKT1, AKT2 and AKT3) called the AKT kinase, and which regulate many processes including metabolism, proliferation, cell survival, growth and angiogenesis. This is mediated through serine and/or threonine phosphorylation of a range of downstream substrates.</data>
