                  <data key="d100">Guanine nucleotide-binding protein G(s) subunit alpha isoforms short</data>
                  <data key="d101">Adenylate cyclase-stimulating G alpha protein</data>
                  <data key="d104">Guanine nucleotide-binding proteins (G proteins) function as transducers in numerous signaling pathways controlled by G protein-coupled receptors (GPCRs). The alpha chain contains the guanine nucleotide binding site and alternates between an active, GTP-bound state and an inactive, GDP-bound state.</data>
